  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Sets: union and intersection</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core and Essential 1.1 (c): List the union and the intersection of two sets, one given by a rule, and count the union.</p><p id="edition">Core and Essential</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Chapter 11, Exercise B, questions 1 and 2 of School Mathematics Project, SMP Book 3 (Metric), ed. A. G. Howson, Cambridge University Press, 1967: listing the intersection and the union of two sets; every pair of sets is new and the count of the union is added.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core and Essential Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
